        "userMessage": "Conversation info (untrusted metadata): ```json { \"message_id\": \"19103\", \"reply_to_id\": \"19101\", \"sender_id\": \"8518484672\", \"sender\": \"Jonathan\", \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-04-15 03:31 PDT\", \"has_reply_context\": true } ``` Sender (untrusted metadata): ```json { \"label\": \"Jonathan (8518484672)\", \"id\": \"8518484672\", \"name\": \"Jonathan\" } ``` Replied message (untrusted, for context): ```json { \"sender_label\": \"pelican\", \"body\": \"Yes. I found a real structural blocker.\\n\\nThis is the clean root cause:\\n\\n1. Live production still generates credit spreads upstream\\n • production_engine.py literally calls find_credit_spreads(...)\\n • the comment there still says “Find credit spreads”\\n2. That function explicitly narrows to only two structures\\n • strategy_sweep.py -> find_credit_spreads() passes:\\n • allowed_spread_types=(\\\"bull_put\\\", \\\"bear_call\\\")\\n3. The menu selector hardcodes the same two-structure subset\\n • cdf_strike_selector.py has:\\n • TIERED_VERTICAL_V1_ALLOWED_STRUCTURES = (\\\"bull_put\\\", \\\"bear_call\\\")\\n • so even though .trigger_config.json says all four are allowed, the selector normalizes back to just those two\\n\\nWhat the logs say:\\n\\n• Across the 2026-04-14 live production decision files, I only found:\\n • bull_put\\n • bear_call\\n• I found zero bull_call\\n• I found zero bear_put\\n• Example: decisions_20260414_150140_775552.json had 21 bear_call and 8 bull_put, nothing else.\\n• Same story in the broker/execution ledger yesterday: only bull_put and bear_call hit live execution.\\n\\nSo the honest answer is:\\n\\n• No, this is not mainly a sizing-floor or quality-floor problem for the missing two structures.\\n• Bull_call and bear_put are mostly not reaching the live funnel at all.\\n• The one rejection I saw yesterday was PYPL bull_put = edge_below_tier1, which is a normal post-selection rejection inside the two-structure world.\\n\\nBluntly:\\n\\n• Config says four\\n• Live upstream selector still behaves like two\\n• So yes, it is partially broken / half-wired\\n\\nThe good news:\\n\\n• downstream code in run_once.py and order_manager.py does have debit-handling logic\\n• so this looks like an upstream candidate-generation / menu-selection seam, not a total rewrite\\n\\nIf you want, I can take the narrow fix next:\\n\\n• make live candidate generation truly emit all four structures\\n• prove bull_call and bear_put appear in fresh decision files before market open\\n• then check whether any second blocker remains after that\" } ``` We need to deeply and thoroughly fix this!",
